  'ia.sys.etiquettes-documents': 'Give a document’s tags with the AI, when the first pass is not sure',
  'ia.wf.action.tags': 'Give a document’s tags with the AI',
  'ia.wf.action.tags.desc': 'When the first pass without AI did not read them surely: the start of the document’s text and the tags already used in the library are given to the AI. Certain: its tags (at most six) are given (“given by the AI”), if the document says them or the library already uses them; otherwise they stay to confirm.',
  'ia.wf.tags.system': 'You read the start of a document to give it 3 to 6 tags: short keywords (one to three words, lower case) that say its subject. Prefer the tags already used in the library when they fit, written exactly as they are: {list}. Otherwise, take words from the document itself; invent nothing. Answer in JSON: tags — the list of tags —, and certain: true only if the document clearly shows its subject.',
